{
  "title": "40: Ghafir غافر",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nحٰمٓ‌ ۚ‏(1)\nHAA MEEM.\nHa, Meem.\nتَنْزِيْلُ الْكِتٰبِ مِنَ اللّٰهِ الْعَزِيْزِ الْعَلِيْمِۙ‏(2)\nTANZEELUL KETAABE MENAL LAAHIL A’ZEEZIL A’LEEM.\nThe [gradual] sending down of the Book is from Allah, the All-mighty, the All-knowing,\nغَافِرِ الذَّنْۢبِ وَقَابِلِ التَّوْبِ شَدِيْدِ الْعِقَابِ ذِى الطَّوْلِؕ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَؕ اِلَيْهِ الْمَصِيْرُ‏(3)\nGHAAFERIZ ZAMBE WA QAABELIT TAWBE SHADEEDIL E’QAABE ZIT TAWL, LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOO, ELAYHIL MASEER.\nforgiver of sins and acceptor of repentance, severe in retribution, [yet] all-bountiful; there is no god except Him, [and] toward Him is the destination.\nمَا يُجَادِلُ فِىْۤ اٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ اِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا فَلَا يَغْرُرْكَ تَقَلُّبُهُمْ فِى الْبِلَادِ‏(4)\nMAA YOJAADELO FEE AAYAATIL LAAHE ILLAL LAZEENA KAFAROO FALAA YAGHRURKA TAQALLOBOHUM FIL BELAAD.\nNo one disputes the signs of Allah except the faithless. So do not be misled by their bustle in the towns.\nكَذَّبَتْ قَبْلَهُمْ قَوْمُ نُوْحٍ وَّ الْاَحْزَابُ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْ وَهَمَّتْ كُلُّ اُمَّةٍۢ بِرَسُوْلِهِمْ لِيَاْخُذُوْهُ ؕ وَجَادَلُوْا بِالْبَاطِلِ لِيُدْحِضُوْا بِهِ الْحَقَّ فَاَخَذْتُهُمْ فَكَيْفَ كَانَ عِقَابِ‏(5)\nKAZZABAT QABLAHUM QAWMO NOOHINW WAL AHZAABO MIM BA’DEHIM, WA HAMMAT KULLO UMMATIM BE-RASOOLEHIM LE-YAAKHOZOOH, WA JAADALOO BIL-BAATELE LE-YUDHEZOO BEHIL HAQQA FA-AKHAZTOHUM, FAKAYFA KAANA E’QAAB.\nThe people of Noah denied before them and the [heathen] factions [who came] after them. Every nation attempted to lay hands on their apostle, and disputed erroneously to refute the truth. Then I seized them; so how was My retribution?!\nوَكَذٰلِكَ حَقَّتْ كَلِمَتُ رَبِّكَ عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اَنَّهُمْ اَصْحٰبُ النَّارِ ‌ۘ‏(6)\nWA KAZAALEKA HAQQAT KALEMATO RABBEKA A’LAL LAZEENA KAFAROO ANNAHUM ASHAABUN NAAR.\nThat is how the word of your Lord became due concerning the faithless, that they shall be inmates of the Fire.\nاَلَّذِيْنَ يَحْمِلُوْنَ الْعَرْشَ وَمَنْ حَوْلَهٗ يُسَبِّحُوْنَ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّهِمْ وَيُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِهٖ وَيَسْتَغْفِرُوْنَ لِلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا‌ ۚ رَبَّنَا وَسِعْتَ كُلَّ شَىْءٍ رَّحْمَةً وَّعِلْمًا فَاغْفِرْ لِلَّذِيْنَ تَابُوْا وَاتَّبَعُوْا سَبِيْلَكَ وَقِهِمْ عَذَابَ الْجَحِيْمِ‏(7)\nLAZEENA YAHMELOONAL A’RSHA WA MAN HAWLAHU YOSABBEHOONA BE-HAMDE RABBEHIM WA YOAMENOONA BEHI WA YASTAGHFEROONA LILLAZEENA AAMANOO, RABBANAA WASE’TA KULLA SHAY-IR RAHMATANW WA I’LMAN FAGHFIR LILLAZEENA TAABOO WAT TABA-O’O SABEELAKA WA QEHIM A’ZAABAL JAHEEM.\nThose who bear the Throne, and those who are around it, celebrate the praise of their Lord and have faith in Him, and they plead for forgiveness for the faithful: ‘Our Lord! You embrace all things in mercy and knowledge. So forgive those who repent and follow Your way and save them from the punishment of hell.\nرَبَّنَا وَاَدْخِلْهُمْ جَنّٰتِ عَدْنِ اۨلَّتِىْ وَعَدْتَّهُمْ وَمَنْ صَلَحَ مِنْ اٰبَآئِهِمْ وَاَزْوَاجِهِمْ وَذُرِّيّٰتِهِمْ ؕ اِنَّكَ اَنْتَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ ۙ‏(8)\nRABBANAA WA ADKHILHUM JANNAATE A’DNENIL LATEE WA-A’TTAHUM WA MAN SALAHA MIN AABAAA-EHIM WA AZWAAJEHIM WA ZURRIYYAATEHIM, INNAKA ANTAL A’ZEEZUL HAKEEM.\nOur Lord! Admit them into the Gardens of Eden, which You have promised them, along with whoever is righteous among their forebears, their spouses and their descendants. Indeed You are the All-mighty, the All-wise.\nوَقِهِمُ السَّيِّاٰتِ ؕ وَمَنْ تَقِ السَّيِّاٰتِ يَوْمَئِذٍ فَقَدْ رَحِمْتَهٗ ؕ وَذٰ لِكَ هُوَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيْمُ‏(9)\nWA QEHEMUS SAYYE-AAT, WA MAN TAQIS SAYYE-AATE YAWMA-EZIN FAQAD RAHIMTAH, WA ZAALEKA HOWAL FAWZUL A’ZEEM.\nSave them from the ills [of the Day of Retribution]; and whomever You save from the ills that day, You will have had mercy upon him, and that is the great triumph.’\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا يُنَادَوْنَ لَمَقْتُ اللّٰهِ اَكْبَرُ مِنْ مَّقْتِكُمْ اَنْفُسَكُمْ اِذْ تُدْعَوْنَ اِلَى الْاِيْمَانِ فَتَكْفُرُوْنَ‏(10)\nINNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO YONAADAWNA LA-MAQTUL LAAHE AKBARO MIM MAQTEKUM ANFOSAKUM IZ TUD-A’WNA ELAL EEMAANE FA-TAKFOROON.\nIt will be proclaimed to the faithless: ‘Surely, Allah’s outrage [towards you] is greater than your outrage towards yourselves, as you were invited to faith, but you disbelieved.’\nقَالُوْا رَبَّنَاۤ اَمَتَّنَا اثْنَتَيْنِ وَاَحْيَيْتَنَا اثْنَتَيْنِ فَاعْتَرَفْنَا بِذُنُوْبِنَا فَهَلْ اِلٰى خُرُوْجٍ مِّنْ سَبِيْلٍ‏(11)\nQAALOO RABBANAA AMATTANAS NATAYNE WA AHYAYTANAS NATAYNE FA’TARAFNAA BE-ZONOOBENAA FAHAL ELAA KHOROOJIM MIN SABEEL.\nThey will say, ‘Our Lord! Twice did You make us die, and twice did You give us life. We admit our sins. Is there any way out [from this plight]?’\nذٰ لِكُمْ بِاَنَّهٗۤ اِذَا دُعِىَ اللّٰهُ وَحْدَهٗ كَفَرْتُمْ ۚ وَاِنْ يُّشْرَكْ بِهٖ تُؤْمِنُوْا ؕ فَالْحُكْمُ لِلّٰهِ الْعَلِىِّ الْكَبِيْرِ‏(12)\nZAALEKUM BE-ANNAHU EZAA DO-E’YAL LAAHO WAHDAHU KAFARTUM, WA IN-Y YUSHRAK BEHI TOAMENOO, FALHUKMO LILLAAHIL A’LIYYIL KABEER.\n[They will be told,] ‘This [plight of yours] is because, when Allah was invoked alone, you would disbelieve, but if partners were ascribed to Him you would believe. So the judgment belongs to Allah, the All-exalted, the All-great.’\nهُوَ الَّذِىْ يُرِيْكُمْ اٰيٰتِهٖ وَيُنَزِّلُ لَكُمْ مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ رِزْقًا ؕ وَمَا يَتَذَكَّرُ اِلَّا مَنْ يُّنِيْبُ‏(13)\nHOWAL LAZEE YOREEKUM AAYAATEHI WA YONAZZELO LAKUM MENAS SAMAAA-E RIZQAA, WA MAA YATAZAKKARO ILLAA MAN-Y YONEEB.\nIt is He who shows you His signs and sends down provision for you from the sky. Yet no one takes admonition except those who return penitently [to Allah].\nفَادْعُوا اللّٰهَ مُخْلِصِيْنَ لَهُ الدِّيْنَ وَلَوْ كَرِهَ الْكٰفِرُوْنَ‏(14)\nFAD-U’L LAAHA MUKHLESEENA LAHUD DEENA WA LAW KAREHAL KAAFEROON.\nSo supplicate Allah, putting exclusive faith in Him, though the faithless should be averse.\nرَفِيْعُ الدَّرَجٰتِ ذُو الْعَرْشِ‌ ۚ يُلْقِى الرُّوْحَ مِنْ اَمْرِهٖ عَلٰى مَنْ يَّشَآءُ مِنْ عِبَادِهٖ لِيُنْذِرَ يَوْمَ التَّلَاقِ ۙ‏(15)\nRAFEE-U’D DARAJAATE ZUL A’RSH, YULQIR ROOHA MIN AMREHI A’LAA MAN-Y YASHAAA-O MIN E’BAADEHI LE-YUNZERA YAWMAT TALAAQ.\nRaiser of ranks, Lord of the Throne, He casts the Spirit of His command upon whomever of His servants that He wishes, that he may warn [people] of the Day of Encounter.\nيَوْمَ هُمْ بَارِزُوْنَ ۚ لَا يَخْفٰى عَلَى اللّٰهِ مِنْهُمْ شَىْءٌ ؕ لِمَنِ الْمُلْكُ الْيَوْمَ ؕ لِلّٰهِ الْوَاحِدِ الْقَهَّارِ‏(16)\nYAWMA HUM BAAREZOON, LAA YAKHFAA A’LAL LAAHE MINHUM SHAY, LEMANIL MULKUL YAWM, LILLAAHIL WAAHEDIL QAHHAAR.\nThe day when they will emerge [from their graves], nothing about them will be hidden from Allah. ‘To whom does the sovereignty belong today?’ ‘To Allah, the One, the All-paramount!’\nاَ لْيَوْمَ تُجْزٰى كُلُّ نَفْسٍۢ بِمَا كَسَبَتْ ؕ لَا ظُلْمَ الْيَوْمَ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ سَرِيْعُ الْحِسَابِ‏(17)\nAL-YAWMA TUJZAA KULLO NAFSIM BEMAA KASABAT, LAA ZULMAL YAWM, INNAL LAAHA SAREE-U’L HESAAB.\n‘Today every soul shall be requited for what it has earned. There will be no injustice today. Indeed Allah is swift at reckoning.’\nوَاَنْذِرْهُمْ يَوْمَ الْاٰزِفَةِ اِذِ الْقُلُوْبُ لَدَى الْحَنَاجِرِ كٰظِمِيْنَ ؕ مَا لِلظّٰلِمِيْنَ مِنْ حَمِيْمٍ وَّلَا شَفِيْعٍ يُّطَاعُ ؕ‏(18)\nWA ANZIRHUM YAWMAL AAZEFATE EZIL QOLOOBO LADAL HANAAJERE KAAZEMEEN, MAA LIZ-ZAALEMEENA MIN HAMEEMINW WA LAA SHAFEE-I’N-Y YOTAA’.\nWarn them of the Approaching Day, when the hearts will be at the throats, choking with suppressed agony, [and] the wrongdoers will have no sympathizer, nor any intercessor who might be heard.\nيَعْلَمُ خَآئِنَةَ الْاَعْيُنِ وَمَا تُخْفِى الصُّدُوْرُ‏(19)\nYA’LAMO KHAAA-ENATAL A-A’YONE WA MAA TUKHFIS SODOOR.\nHe knows the treachery of the eyes, and what the breasts hide.\nوَاللّٰهُ يَقْضِىْ بِالْحَقِّؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ يَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِهٖ لَا يَقْضُوْنَ بِشَىْءٍؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْبَصِيْرُ‏(20)\nWAL LAAHO YAQZEE BIL-HAQ, WAL LAZEENA YAD-O’ONA MIN DOONEHI LAA YAQZOONA BE-SHAY, INNAL LAAHA HOWAS SAMEE-U’L BASEER.\nAllah judges with justice, while those whom they invoke besides Him do not judge by anything. Indeed it is Allah who is the All-hearing, the All-seeing.\nاَوَلَمْ يَسِيْرُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ فَيَنْظُرُوْا كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الَّذِيْنَ كَانُوْا مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْؕ كَانُوْا هُمْ اَشَدَّ مِنْهُمْ قُوَّةً وَّاٰثَارًا فِى الْاَرْضِ فَاَخَذَهُمُ اللّٰهُ بِذُنُوْبِهِمْؕ وَمَا كَانَ لَهُمْ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ مِنْ وَّاقٍ‏(21)\nAWA LAM YASEEROO FIL ARZE FA-YANZOROO KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATUL LAZEENA KAANOO MIN QABLEHIM, KAANOO HUM ASHADDA MINHUM QUWWATANW WA AASAARAN FIL ARZE FA-AKHAZAHOMUL LAAHO BE-ZONOOBEHIM, WA MAA KAANA LAHUM MENAL LAAHE MINW WAAQ.\nHave they not travelled through the land so that they may observe how was the fate of those who were before them? They were greater than them in might and with respect to the effects [they left] in the land. But then Allah seized them for their sins, and they had no defender against Allah [’s punishment].\nذٰلِكَ بِاَنَّهُمْ كَانَتْ تَّاْتِيْهِمْ رُسُلُهُمْ بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ فَكَفَرُوْا فَاَخَذَهُمُ اللّٰهُؕ اِنَّهٗ قَوِىٌّ شَدِيْدُ الْعِقَابِ‏(22)\nZAALEKA BE-ANNAHUM KAANAT TAATEEHIM ROSOLOHUM BIL-BAYYENAATE FA-KAFAROO FA-AKHAZAHOMUL LAAH, INNAHU QAWIYYUN SHADEEDUL E’QAAB.\nThat was because their apostles used to bring them manifest proofs, but they defied [them]. So Allah seized them. Indeed He is all-strong, severe in retribution.\nوَلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا مُوْسٰى بِاٰيٰتِنَا وَسُلْطٰنٍ مُّبِيْنٍۙ‏(23)\nWA LAQAD ARSALNAA MOOSAA BE-AAYAATENAA WA SULTAANIM MOBEEN.\nCertainly We sent Moses with Our signs and a manifest authority\nاِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ وَ هَامٰنَ وَقَارُوْنَ فَقَالُوْا سٰحِرٌ كَذَّابٌ‏(24)\nELAA FIR-A’WNA WA HAAMAANA WA QAAROONA FA-QAALOO SAAHERUN KAZZAAB.\nto Pharaoh, Haman and Korah, but they said, ‘A magician and a mendacious liar.’\nفَلَمَّا جَآءَهُمْ بِالْحَقِّ مِنْ عِنْدِنَا قَالُوْا اقْتُلُوْۤا اَبْنَآءَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مَعَهٗ وَاسْتَحْيُوْا نِسَآءَهُمْؕ وَمَا كَيْدُ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ اِلَّا فِىْ ضَلٰلٍ‏(25)\nFALAMMAA JAAA-AHUM BIL-HAQQE MIN I’NDENAA QAALUQ TOLOO ABNAAA-AL LAZEENA AAMANOO MA-A’HU WAS TAHYOO NESAAA-AHUM, WA MAA KAYDUL KAAFEREENA ILLAA FEE ZALAAL.\nSo when he brought them the truth from Us, they said, ‘Kill the sons of the faithful who are with him, and spare their women.’ But the stratagems of the faithless only go awry.\nوَقَالَ فِرْعَوْنُ ذَرُوْنِىْۤ اَقْتُلْ مُوْسٰى وَلْيَدْعُ رَبَّهٗ‌ۚ اِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ اَنْ يُّبَدِّلَ دِيْنَكُمْ اَوْ اَنْ يُّظْهِرَ فِى الْاَرْضِ الْفَسَادَ‏(26)\nWA QAALA FIR-A’WNO ZAROONEE AQTUL MOOSAA WAL YAD-O’ RABBAH, INNEE AKHAAFO AN-Y YOBADDELA DEENAKUM AW AN-Y YUZHERA FIL ARZIL FASAAD.\nAnd Pharaoh said, ‘Let me slay Moses, and let him invoke his Lord. Indeed I fear that he will change your religion, or bring forth corruption in our land.’\nوَقَالَ مُوْسٰٓى اِنِّىْ عُذْتُ بِرَبِّىْ وَرَبِّكُمْ مِّنْ كُلِّ مُتَكَبِّرٍ لَّا يُؤْمِنُ بِيَوْمِ الْحِسَابِ‏(27)\nWA QAALA MOOSAA INNEE U’ZTO BE-RABBEE WA RABBEKUM MIN KULLE MOTAKABBERIL LAA YOAMENO BE-YAWMIL HESAAB.\nMoses said, ‘I seek the protection of my Lord and your Lord from every arrogant one who does not believe in the Day of Reckoning.’\nوَقَالَ رَجُلٌ مُّؤْمِنٌ ‌ۖ مِّنْ اٰلِ فِرْعَوْنَ يَكْتُمُ اِيْمَانَهٗۤ اَتَقْتُلُوْنَ رَجُلًا اَنْ يَّقُوْلَ رَبِّىَ اللّٰهُ وَقَدْ جَآءَكُمْ بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ مِنْ رَّبِّكُمْ ؕ وَاِنْ يَّكُ كَاذِبًا فَعَلَيْهِ كَذِبُهٗ ؕ وَاِنْ يَّكُ صَادِقًا يُّصِبْكُمْ بَعْضُ الَّذِىْ يَعِدُكُمْ ۚ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَهْدِىْ مَنْ هُوَ مُسْرِفٌ كَذَّابٌ‏(28)\nWA QAALA RAJOLUM MOAMEN, MIN AALE FIR-A’WNA YAKTOMO EEMAANAHU ATAQTOLOONA RAJOLAN AN-Y YAQOOLA RABBEYAL LAAHO WA QAD JAAA-AKUM BIL-BAYYENAATE MIR RABBEKUM, WA IN-Y YAKO KAAZEBAN FA-A’LAYHE KAZEBOH, WA IN-Y YAKO SAADEQAN-Y YOSIBKUM BA’ZUL LAZEE YA-E’DOKUM, INNAL LAAHA LAA YAHDEE MAN HOWA MUSREFUN KAZZAAB.\nSaid a man of faith from Pharaoh’s clan, who concealed his faith, ‘Will you kill a man for saying, ‘‘My Lord is Allah,’’ while he has already brought you manifest proofs from your Lord? Should he be lying, his falsehood will be to his own detriment; but if he is truthful, there shall visit you some of what he promises you. Indeed Allah does not guide someone who is a transgressor and liar.\nيٰقَوْمِ لَكُمُ الْمُلْكُ الْيَوْمَ ظٰهِرِيْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ فَمَنْ يَّنْصُرُنَا مِنْۢ بَاْسِ اللّٰهِ اِنْ جَآءَنَا ؕ قَالَ فِرْعَوْنُ مَاۤ اُرِيْكُمْ اِلَّا مَاۤ اَرٰى وَمَاۤ اَهْدِيْكُمْ اِلَّا سَبِيْلَ الرَّشَادِ‏(29)\nYAA QAWME LAKOMUL MULKUL YAWMA ZAAHEREENA FIL ARZ, FAMAN-Y YANSORONAA MIM BAASIL LAAHE IN JAAA-ANAA, QAALA FIR-A’WNO MAA OREEKUM ILLAA MAA ARAA WA MAA AHDEEKUM ILLAA SABEELAR RASHAAD.\nO my people! Today sovereignty belongs to you, and you are dominant in the land. But who will save us from Allah’s punishment should it overtake us?’ Pharaoh said, ‘I just point out to you what I see [to be advisable for you], and I guide you only to the way of rectitude.’\nوَقَالَ الَّذِىْۤ اٰمَنَ يٰقَوْمِ اِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ عَلَيْكُمْ مِّثْلَ يَوْمِ الْاَحْزَابِۙ‏(30)\nWA QAALAL LAZEE AAMANA YAA QAWME INNEE AKHAAFO A’LAYKUM MISLA YAWMIL AHZAAB.\nHe who had faith said, ‘O my people! Indeed I fear for you [a day] like the day of the [heathen] factions;\nمِثْلَ دَاْبِ قَوْمِ نُوْحٍ وَّعَادٍ وَّثَمُوْدَ وَالَّذِيْنَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْؕ وَمَا اللّٰهُ يُرِيْدُ ظُلْمًا لِّلْعِبَادِ‏(31)\nMISLA DAABE QAWME NOOHINW WA A’ADINW WA SAMOODA WAL LAZEENA MIM BA’DEHIM, WA MAL LAAHO YOREEDO ZULMAL LIL-E’BAAD.\nlike the case of the people of Noah, of Ad and Thamud, and those who came after them, and Allah does not desire any wrong for [His] servants.\nوَيٰقَوْمِ اِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ عَلَيْكُمْ يَوْمَ التَّنَادِۙ‏(32)\nWA YAA QAWME INNEE AKHAAFO A’LAYKUM YAWMAT TANAAD.\nO my people! I fear for you a day of mutual distress calls,\nيَوْمَ تُوَلُّوْنَ مُدْبِرِيْنَ‌ۚ مَا لَكُمْ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ مِنْ عَاصِمٍۚ وَمَنْ يُّضْلِلِ اللّٰهُ فَمَا لَهٗ مِنْ هَادٍ‏(33)\nYAWMA TOWALLOONA MUDBEREEN, MAA LAKUM MENAL LAAHE MIN A’ASEM, WA MAN-Y YUZLELIL LAAHO FAMAA LAHU MIN HAAD.\na day when you will turn back [to flee], not having anyone to protect you from Allah, and whomever Allah leads astray has no guide.\nوَلَقَدْ جَآءَكُمْ يُوْسُفُ مِنْ قَبْلُ بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ فَمَا زِلْتُمْ فِىْ شَكٍّ مِّمَّا جَآءَكُمْ بِهٖ ؕ حَتّٰٓى اِذَا هَلَكَ قُلْتُمْ لَنْ يَّبْعَثَ اللّٰهُ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهٖ رَسُوْلًا ؕ كَذٰلِكَ يُضِلُّ اللّٰهُ مَنْ هُوَ مُسْرِفٌ مُّرْتَابٌ  ۚ ۖ‏(34)\nWA LAQAD JAAA-AKUM YOOSOFO MIN QABLO BIL-BAYYENAATE FAMAA ZILTUM FEE SHAKKIM MIMMAA JAAA-AKUM BEH, HATTAA EZAA HALAKA QULTUM LAN-Y YAB-A’SAL LAAHO MIM BA’DEHI RASOOLAA, KAZAALEKA YOZILLUL LAAHO MAN HOWA MUSREFUM MURTAAB.\nCertainly Joseph brought you manifest proofs earlier, but you continued to remain in doubt concerning what he had brought you. When he died, you said, ‘‘Allah will never send any apostle after him.’’ That is how Allah leads astray those who are unrestrained and skeptical.\nاۨلَّذِيْنَ يُجَادِلُوْنَ فِىْۤ اٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ بِغَيْرِ سُلْطٰنٍ اَتٰٮهُمْ ؕ كَبُرَ مَقْتًا عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ وَعِنْدَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا ؕ كَذٰلِكَ يَطْبَعُ اللّٰهُ عَلٰى كُلِّ قَلْبِ مُتَكَبِّرٍ جَبَّارٍ‏(35)\nLAZEENA YOJAADELOONA FEE AAYAATIL LAAHE BE-GHAYRE SULTAANIN ATAAHUM, KABORA MAQTAN I’NDAL LAAHE WA I’NDAL LAZEENA AAMANOO, KAZAALEKA YATBA-U’L LAAHO A’LAA KULLE QALBE MOTAKABBERIN JABBAAR.\nThose who dispute the signs of Allah without any authority that may have come to them—[that is] greatly outrageous to Allah and to those who have faith. That is how Allah seals the heart of every arrogant tyrant.’\nوَقَالَ فِرْعَوْنُ يٰهَامٰنُ ابْنِ لِىْ صَرْحًا لَّعَلِّىْۤ اَبْلُغُ الْاَسْبَابَۙ‏(36)\nWA QAALA FIR-A’WNO YAA HAAMAANUB NE LEE SARHAL LA-A’LLEE ABLOGHUL ASBAAB.\nPharaoh said, ‘O Haman! Build me a tower so that I may reach the routes\nاَسْبَابَ السَّمٰوٰتِ فَاَطَّلِعَ اِلٰٓى اِلٰهِ مُوْسٰى وَاِنِّىْ لَاَظُنُّهٗ كَاذِبًا ؕ وَكَذٰلِكَ زُيِّنَ لِفِرْعَوْنَ سُوْٓءُ عَمَلِهٖ وَصُدَّ عَنِ السَّبِيْلِ ؕ وَمَا كَيْدُ فِرْعَوْنَ اِلَّا فِىْ تَبَابٍ‏(37)\nASBAABAS SAMAAWAATE FA-ATTALE-A’ ELAA ELAAHE MOOSAA WA INNEE LA-AZUNNOHU KAAZEBAA, WA KAZAALEKA ZUYYENA LE-FIR-A’WNA SOO-O A’MALEHI WA SUDDA A’NIS SABEEL, WA MAA KAYDO FIR-A’WNA ILLAA FEE TABAAB.\n—the routes of the heavens—and take a look at the God of Moses, and indeed I consider him a liar.’ The evil of his conduct was thus presented as decorous to Pharaoh, and he was kept from the way [of Allah]. Pharaoh’s stratagems only led him into ruin.\nوَقَالَ الَّذِىْۤ اٰمَنَ يٰقَوْمِ اتَّبِعُوْنِ اَهْدِكُمْ سَبِيْلَ الرَّشَادِ‌ۚ‏(38)\nWA QAALAL LAZEE AAMANA YAA QAWMIT TABE-O’ONE AHDEKUM SABEELAR RASHAAD.\nAnd he who had faith said, ‘O my people! Follow me; I will guide you to the way of rectitude.\nيٰقَوْمِ اِنَّمَا هٰذِهِ الْحَيٰوةُ الدُّنْيَا مَتَاعٌ وَّاِنَّ الْاٰخِرَةَ هِىَ دَارُ الْقَرَارِ‏(39)\nYAA QAWME INNAMAA HAAZEHIL HAYAATUD DUNYAA MATAA’, WA INNAL AAKHERATA HEYA DAARUL QARAAR.\nO my people! This life of the world is only a [passing] enjoyment, and indeed the Hereafter is the abiding home.\nمَنْ عَمِلَ سَيِّئَةً فَلَا يُجْزٰٓى اِلَّا مِثْلَهَا ۚ وَمَنْ عَمِلَ صَالِحًا مِّنْ ذَكَرٍ اَوْ اُنْثٰى وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ يَدْخُلُوْنَ الْجَنَّةَ يُرْزَقُوْنَ فِيْهَا بِغَيْرِ حِسَابٍ‏(40)\nMAN A’MELA SAYYE-ATAN FALAA YUJZAA ILLAA MISLAHAA, WA MAN A’MELA SAALEHAM MIN ZAKARIN AW UNSAA WA HOWA MOAMENUN FA-OOLAAA-EKA YADKHOLOONAL JANNATA YURZAQOONA FEEHAA BE-GHAYRE HESAAB.\nWhoever commits a misdeed shall not be requited except with its like, but whoever acts righteously, whether male or female, should he be faithful—such shall enter paradise, and they will be provided therein without any reckoning.\nوَيٰقَوْمِ مَا لِىْۤ اَدْعُوْكُمْ اِلَى النَّجٰوةِ وَتَدْعُوْنَنِىْۤ اِلَى النَّارِؕ‏(41)\nWA YAA QAWME MAA LEE AD-O’OKUM ELAN NAJAATE WA TAD-O’ONANEE ELAN NAAR.\nO my people! [Think,] what makes me invite you to deliverance, while you invite me toward the Fire?\nتَدْعُوْنَنِىْ لِاَكْفُرَ بِاللّٰهِ وَاُشْرِكَ بِهٖ مَا لَيْسَ لِىْ بِهٖ عِلْمٌ وَّاَنَا اَدْعُوْكُمْ اِلَى الْعَزِيْزِ الْغَفَّارِ‏(42)\nTAD-O’ONANEE LE-AKFORA BIL-LAAHE WA USHREKA BEHI MAA LAYSA LEE BEHI I’LM, WA ANAA AD-O’OKUM ELAL A’ZEEZIL GHAFFAAR.\nYou invite me to defy Allah and to ascribe to Him partners of which I have no knowledge, while I call you to the All-mighty, the All-forgiver.\nلَا جَرَمَ اَنَّمَا تَدْعُوْنَنِىْۤ اِلَيْهِ لَيْسَ لَهٗ دَعْوَةٌ فِى الدُّنْيَا وَلَا فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ وَاَنَّ مَرَدَّنَاۤ اِلَى اللّٰهِ وَاَنَّ الْمُسْرِفِيْنَ هُمْ اَصْحٰبُ النَّارِ‏(43)\nLAA JARAMA ANNAMAA TAD-O’ONANEE ELAYHE LAYSA LAHU DA’WATUN FID DUNYAA WA LAA FIL AAKHERATE WA ANNA MARADDANAA ELAL LAAHE WA ANNAL MUSREFEENA HUM ASHAABUN NAAR.\nUndoubtedly, that to which you invite me has no invitation in the world nor in the Hereafter, and indeed our return will be to Allah, and indeed it is the transgressors who will be inmates of the Fire.\nفَسَتَذْكُرُوْنَ مَاۤ اَقُوْلُ لَكُمْؕ وَاُفَوِّضُ اَمْرِىْۤ اِلَى اللّٰهِؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ بَصِيْرٌۢ بِالْعِبَادِ‏(44)\nFASATAZKOROONA MAA AQOOLO LAKUM, WA OFAWWEZO AMREE ELAL LAAH, INNAL LAAHA BASEERUM BIL-E’BAAD.\nSoon you will remember what I tell you, and I entrust my affair to Allah. Indeed Allah watches His servants.’\nفَوَقٰٮهُ اللّٰهُ سَيِّاٰتِ مَا مَكَرُوْا وَحَاقَ بِاٰلِ فِرْعَوْنَ سُوْٓءُ الْعَذَابِ‌ۚ‏(45)\nFA-WAQAAHUL LAAHO SAYYE-AATE MAA MAKAROO WA HAAQA BE-AALE FIR-A’WNA SOO-UL A’ZAAB.\nThen Allah saved him from their evil schemes, while a terrible punishment besieged Pharaoh’s clan:\nاَلنَّارُ يُعْرَضُوْنَ عَلَيْهَا غُدُوًّا وَّعَشِيًّا ۚ وَيَوْمَ تَقُوْمُ السَّاعَةُ اَدْخِلُوْۤا اٰلَ فِرْعَوْنَ اَشَدَّ الْعَذَابِ‏(46)\nNAARO YO’RAZOONA A’LAYHAA GHODUWWANW WA A’SHIYYAA, WA YAWMA TAQOOMUS SAA-A’H, ADKHELOO AALA FIR-A’WNA ASHADDAL A’ZAAB.\nthe Fire, to which they are exposed morning and evening. On the day when the Hour sets in, Pharaoh’s clan will enter the severest punishment.\nوَاِذْ يَتَحَآجُّوْنَ فِى النَّارِ فَيَقُوْلُ الضُّعَفٰٓؤُا لِلَّذِيْنَ اسْتَكْبَرُوْۤا اِنَّا كُنَّا لَكُمْ تَبَعًا فَهَلْ اَنْتُمْ مُّغْنُوْنَ عَنَّا نَصِيْبًا مِّنَ النَّارِ‏(47)\nWA IZ YATAHAAJJOONA FIN NAARE FA-YAQOOLUZ ZO-A’FAAA-O LILLAZEENAS TAKBAROO INNAA KUNNAA LAKUM TABA-A’N FAHAL ANTUM MUGHNOONA A’NNAA NASEEBAM MENAN NAAR.\nWhen they argue in the Fire, the oppressed will say to the oppressors, ‘We used to follow you; will you avail us against any portion of the Fire?’\nقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ اسْتَكْبَرُوْۤا اِنَّا كُلٌّ فِيْهَاۤۙاِنَّ اللّٰهَ قَدْ حَكَمَ بَيْنَ الْعِبَادِ‏(48)\nQAALAL LAZEENAS TAKBAROO INNAA KULLUN FEEHAA, INNAL LAAHA QAD HAKAMA BAYNAL E’BAAD.\nThe oppressors will say, ‘We are all in it [together]; Allah has judged between [His] servants.’\nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ فِى النَّارِ لِخَزَنَةِ جَهَنَّمَ ادْعُوْا رَبَّكُمْ يُخَفِّفْ عَنَّا يَوْمًا مِّنَ الْعَذَابِ‏(49)\nWA QAALAL LAZEENA FIN NAARE LE-KHAZANATE JAHANNAMAD O’O RABBAKUM YOKHAFFIF A’NNAA YAWMAM MENAL A’ZAAB.\nThose who are in the Fire will say to the keepers of hell, ‘Invoke your Lord to lighten for us [at least] a day’s punishment.’\nقَالُوْۤا اَوَلَمْ تَكُ تَاْتِيْكُمْ رُسُلُكُمْ بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ ؕ قَالُوْا بَلٰى ؕ قَالُوْا‌ فَادْعُوْا ۚ وَمَا دُعٰٓؤُا الْكٰفِرِيْنَ اِلَّا فِىْ ضَلٰلٍ‏(50)\nQAALOO AWA LAM TAKO TAATEEKUM ROSOLOKUM BIL-BAYYENAAT, QAALOO BALAA, QAALOO FAD-O’O, WA MAA DO-A’AA-UL KAAFEREENA ILLAA FEE ZALAAL.\nThey will say, ‘Had not your apostles brought you manifest proofs?’ They will say, ‘Yes.’ They will say, ‘Then invoke [Him] yourselves.’ But the invocations of the faithless only go awry.\nاِنَّا لَنَنْصُرُ رُسُلَنَا وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا وَيَوْمَ يَقُوْمُ الْاَشْهَادُ ۙ‏(51)\nINNAA LANANSORO ROSOLANAA WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO FIL HAYAATID DUNYAA WA YAWMA YAQOOMUL ASH-HAAD.\nIndeed We shall help Our apostles and those who have faith in the life of the world and on the day when the witnesses rise up,\nيَوْمَ لَا يَنْفَعُ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ مَعْذِرَتُهُمْ وَلَهُمُ اللَّعْنَةُ وَلَهُمْ سُوْٓءُ الدَّارِ‏(52)\nYAWMA LAA YANFA-U’Z ZAALEMEENA MA’ZERATOHUM WA LAHOMUL LA’NATO WA LAHUM SOO-UD DAAR.\nthe day when the excuses of the wrongdoers will not benefit them, the curse will lie on them, and for them will be the ills of the [ultimate] abode.\nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَا مُوْسَى الْهُدٰى وَاَوْرَثْنَا بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ الْكِتٰبَۙ‏(53)\nWA LAQAD AATAYNAA MOOSAL HODAA WA AWRASNAA BANEE ISRAAA-EELAL KETAAB.\nCertainly We gave guidance to Moses and We gave the Children of Israel the Book as a legacy,\nهُدًى وَّذِكْرٰى لِاُولِى الْاَلْبَابِ‏(54)\nHODANW WA ZIKRAA LE-OOLIL ALBAAB.\nas guidance and admonition for those who possess intellect.\nفَاصْبِرْ اِنَّ وَعْدَ اللّٰهِ حَقٌّ وَّاسْتَغْفِرْ لِذَنْۢبِكَ وَسَبِّحْ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّكَ بِالْعَشِىِّ وَالْاِبْكَارِ‏(55)\nFASBIR INNA WA’DAL LAAHE HAQQUNW WAS TAGHFIR LE-ZAMBEKA WA SABBEH BE-HAMDE RABBEKA BIL-A’SHIYYE WAL IBKAAR.\nSo be patient! Allah’s promise is indeed true. Plead [Allah] for forgiveness of your sin, and celebrate the praise of your Lord morning and evening.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يُجَادِلُوْنَ فِىْۤ اٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ بِغَيْرِ سُلْطٰنٍ اَتٰٮهُمْۙ اِنْ فِىْ صُدُوْرِهِمْ اِلَّا كِبْرٌ مَّا هُمْ بِبَالِغِيْهِؕ فَاسْتَعِذْ بِاللّٰهِؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْبَصِيْرُ‏(56)\nINNAL LAZEENA YOJAADELOONA FEE AAYAATIL LAAHE BE-GHAYRE SULTAANIN ATAAHUM, IN FEE SODOOREHIM ILLAA KIBRUM MAA HUM BE-BAALEGHEEH, FASTA-I’Z BIL-LAAH, INNAHU HOWAS SAMEE-U’L BASEER.\nIndeed those who dispute the signs of Allah without any authority that may have come to them—there is [an ambition for] greatness in their breasts, which they will never attain. So seek the protection of Allah; indeed, He is the All-hearing, the All-seeing.\nلَخَلْقُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ اَكْبَرُ مِنْ خَلْقِ النَّاسِ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(57)\nLA-KHALQUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE AKBARO MIN KHALQIN NAASE WA LAAKINNA AKSARAN NAASE LAA YA’LAMOON.\nThe creation of the heavens and the earth is surely more prodigious than the creation of mankind, but most people do not know.\nوَمَا يَسْتَوِى الْاَعْمٰى وَالْبَصِيْرُ ۙ وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَ عَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ وَلَا الْمُسِىْٓءُ ؕ قَلِيْلًا مَّا تَتَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(58)\nWA MAA YASTAWIL A-A’MAA WAL BASEERO, WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE WA LAL MOSEE, QALEELAM MAA TATAZAKKAROON.\nThe blind one and the seer are not equal, neither are the evildoers and those who have faith and do righteous deeds. Little is the admonition that you take!\nاِنَّ السَّاعَةَ لَاٰتِيَةٌ لَّا رَيْبَ فِيْهَا وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(59)\nINNAS SAA-A’TA LA-AATEYATUL LAA RAYBA FEEHAA WA LAAKINNA AKSARAN NAASE LAA YOAMENOON.\nIndeed the Hour is bound to come; there is no doubt in it. But most people do not believe.\nوَقَالَ رَبُّكُمُ ادْعُوْنِىْۤ اَسْتَجِبْ لَكُمْؕ اِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يَسْتَكْبِرُوْنَ عَنْ عِبَادَتِىْ سَيَدْخُلُوْنَ جَهَنَّمَ دَاخِرِيْنَ‏(60)\nWA QAALA RABBOKOMUD O’ONEE ASTAJIB LAKUM, INNAL LAZEENA YASTAKBEROONA A’N E’BAADATEE SAYADKHOLOONA JAHANNAMA DAAKHEREEN.\nYour Lord has said, ‘Call Me, and I will hear you!’ Indeed those who are disdainful of My worship will enter hell in utter humiliation.\nاَللّٰهُ الَّذِىْ جَعَلَ لَكُمُ الَّيْلَ لِتَسْكُنُوْا فِيْهِ وَالنَّهَارَ مُبْصِرًا ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَذُوْ فَضْلٍ عَلَى النَّاسِ وَ لٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(61)\nALLAAHUL LAZEE JA-A’LA LAKOMUL LAYLA LE-TASKONOO FEEHE WAN NAHAARA MUBSERAA, INNAL LAAHA LA-ZOO FAZLIN A’LAN NAASE WA LAAKINNA AKSARAN NAASE LAA YASHKOROON.\nIt is Allah who made the night for you, that you may rest in it, and the day to provide visibility. Indeed Allah is gracious to mankind, but most people do not give thanks.\nذٰ لِكُمُ اللّٰهُ رَبُّكُمْ خَالِقُ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ‌ ۘ لَّاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ ‌ۚ  فَاَ نّٰى تُؤْفَكُوْنَ‏(62)\nZAALEKOMUL LAAHO RABBOKUM KHAALEQO KULLE SHAY, LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOO, FA-ANNAA TOAFAKOON.\nThat is Allah, your Lord, the creator of all things, there is no god except Him. Then where do you stray?\nكَذٰلِكَ يُؤْفَكُ الَّذِيْنَ كَانُوْا بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ يَجْحَدُوْنَ‏(63)\nKAZAALEKA YOAFAKUL LAZEENA KAANOO BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE YAJHADOON.\nThose who were used to impugning the signs of Allah are thus made to go astray.\nاَللّٰهُ الَّذِىْ جَعَلَ لَكُمُ الْاَرْضَ قَرَارًا وَّالسَّمَآءَ بِنَآءً وَّصَوَّرَكُمْ فَاَحْسَنَ صُوَرَكُمْ وَرَزَقَكُمْ مِّنَ الطَّيِّبٰتِ ؕ ذٰ لِكُمُ اللّٰهُ رَبُّكُمْ ‌ ۖۚ فَتَبٰرَكَ اللّٰهُ رَبُّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(64)\nALLAAHUL LAZEE JA-A’LA LAKOMUL ARZA QARAARANW WAS SAMAAA-A BENAAA-ANW WA SAWWARAKUM FA-AHSANA SOWARAKUM WA RAZAQAKUM MENAT TAYYEBAAT, ZAALEKOMUL LAAHO RABBOKUM, FA-TABAARAKAL LAAHO RABBUL A’ALAMEEN.\nIt is Allah who made for you the earth an abode and the sky a canopy. He formed you and perfected your forms, and provided you with all the good things. That is Allah, your Lord! Blessed is Allah, Lord of all the worlds!\nهُوَ الْحَىُّ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ فَادْعُوْهُ مُخْلِصِيْنَ لَهُ الدِّيْنَؕ اَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(65)\nHOWAL HAYYO LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWA FAD-O’OHO MUKHLESEENA LAHUD DEEN, AL-HAMDO LILLAAHE RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nHe is the Living One, there is no god except Him. So supplicate Him, putting exclusive faith in Him. All praise belongs to Allah, Lord of all the worlds.\nقُلْ اِنِّىْ نُهِيْتُ اَنْ اَعْبُدَ الَّذِيْنَ تَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ لَمَّا جَآءَنِىَ الْبَيِّنٰتُ مِنْ رَّبِّىْ وَاُمِرْتُ اَنْ اُسْلِمَ لِرَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(66)\nQUL INNEE NOHEETO AN A-A’BODAL LAZEENA TAD-O’ONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE LAMMAA JAAA-ANEYAL BAYYENAATO MIR RABBEE, WA OMIRTO AN USLEMA LE-RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nSay, ‘I have been forbidden to worship those whom you invoke besides Allah, as manifest proofs have come to me from my Lord, and I have been commanded to submit to the Lord of all the worlds.’\nهُوَ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَكُمْ مِّنْ تُرَابٍ ثُمَّ مِنْ نُّطْفَةٍ ثُمَّ مِنْ عَلَقَةٍ ثُمَّ يُخْرِجُكُمْ طِفْلًا ثُمَّ لِتَبْلُغُوْۤا اَشُدَّكُمْ ثُمَّ لِتَكُوْنُوْا شُيُوْخًا ؕ وَمِنْكُمْ مَّنْ يُّتَوَفّٰى مِنْ قَبْلُ وَلِتَبْلُغُوْۤا اَجَلًا مُّسَمًّى وَّلَعَلَّكُمْ تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(67)\nHOWAL LAZEE KHALAQAKUM MIN TORAABIN SUMMA MIN NUTFATIN SUMMA MIN A’LAQATIN SUMMA YUKHREJOKUM TIFLAN SUMMA LE-TABLOGHOO ASHUDDAKUM SUMMA LE-TAKOONOO SHOYOOKHAA, WA MINKUM MAN-Y YOTAWAFFAA MIN QABLO WA LE-TABLOGHOO AJALAM MOSAMMANW WA LA-A’LLAKUM TA’QELOON.\nIt is He who created you from dust, then from a drop of [seminal] fluid, then from a clinging mass, then He brings you forth as infants, then [He nurtures you] so that you may come of age, and then that you may become aged—though there are some of you who die earlier—and complete a specified term, and so that you may exercise your reason.\nهُوَ الَّذِىْ يُحْىٖ وَيُمِيْتُؕ فَاِذَا قَضٰٓى اَمْرًا فَاِنَّمَا يَقُوْلُ لَهٗ كُنْ فَيَكُوْنُ‏(68)\nHOWAL LAZEE YOHYEE WA YOMEET, FA-EZAA QAZAA AMRAN FA-INNAMAA YAQOOLO LAHU KUN FA-YAKOON.\nIt is He who gives life and brings death. When He decides on a matter, He just says to it, ‘Be!’ and it is.\nاَلَمْ تَرَ اِلَى الَّذِيْنَ يُجَادِلُوْنَ فِىْۤ اٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِؕ اَنّٰى يُصْرَفُوْنَ  ۛۚ ۙ‏(69)\nALAM TARA ELAL LAZEENA YOJAADELOONA FEE AAYAATIL LAAH, ANNAA YUSRAFOON.\nHave you not regarded those who dispute the signs of Allah, where they are being led away [from Allah’s way]?\nالَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِالْكِتٰبِ وَبِمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا بِهٖ رُسُلَنَا ۛ  فَسَوْفَ يَعْلَمُوْنَ ۙ‏(70)\nLAZEENA KAZZABOO BIL-KETAABE WA BEMAA ARSALNAA BEHI ROSOLANAA, FASAWFA YA’LAMOON.\n—Those who deny the Book and what we have sent with Our apostles. Soon they will know\nاِذِ الْاَغْلٰلُ فِىْۤ اَعْنَاقِهِمْ وَالسَّلٰسِلُؕ يُسْحَبُوْنَۙ‏(71)\nEZIL AGHLAALO FEE A-A’NAAQEHIM WAS SALAASEL, YUSHABOON.\nwhen they are dragged [with] iron collars and chains around their necks\nفِى الْحَمِيْمِ ۙ ثُمَّ فِى النَّارِ يُسْجَرُوْنَ‌ ۚ‏(72)\nFIL HAMEEME, SUMMA FIN NAARE YUSJAROON.\ninto scalding waters and then set aflame in the Fire.\nثُمَّ قِيْلَ لَهُمْ اَيْنَ مَا كُنْتُمْ تُشْرِكُوْنَۙ‏(73)\nSUMMA QEELA LAHUM AYNA MAA KUNTUM TUSHREKOON.\nThen they will be told, ‘Where are they whom you used to worship as deities\nمِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ ؕ قَالُوْا ضَلُّوْا عَنَّا بَلْ لَّمْ نَكُنْ نَّدْعُوْا مِنْ قَبْلُ شَيْئًا ؕ كَذٰلِكَ يُضِلُّ اللّٰهُ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(74)\nMIN DOONIL LAAH, QAALOO ZALLOO A’NNAA BAL LAM NAKUN NAD-O’O MIN QABLO SHAY-AA, KAZAALEKA YOZILLUL LAAHUL KAAFEREEN.\nbesides Allah?’ They will say, ‘They have forsaken us. No, we did not invoke anything before.’ That is how Allah leads the faithless astray.\nذٰ لِكُمْ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَفْرَحُوْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ بِغَيْرِ الْحَقِّ وَبِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَمْرَحُوْنَ‌ ۚ‏(75)\nZAALEKUM BEMAA KUNTUM TAFRAHOONA FIL ARZE BE-GHAYRIL HAQQE WA BEMAA KUNTUM TAMRAHOON.\n‘That [punishment] is because you used to boast unduly on the earth and because you used to strut.\nاُدْخُلُوْۤا اَبْوَابَ جَهَنَّمَ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا ۚ فَبِئْسَ مَثْوَى الْمُتَكَبِّرِيْنَ‏(76)\nUDKHOLOO ABWAABA JAHANNAMA KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA, FA-BEASA MASWAL MOTAKABBEREEN.\nEnter the gates of hell, to remain in it [forever].’ Evil is the [final] abode of the arrogant.\nفَاصْبِرْ اِنَّ وَعْدَ اللّٰهِ حَقٌّۚ فَاِمَّا نُرِيَنَّكَ بَعْضَ الَّذِىْ نَعِدُهُمْ اَوْ نَتَوَفَّيَنَّكَ فَاِلَيْنَا يُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(77)\nFASBIR INNA WA’DAL LAAHE HAQ, FA-IMMAA NOREYANNAKA BA’ZAL LAZEE NA-E’DOHUM AW NATAWAFFAYANNAKA FA-ELAYNAA YURJA-O’ON.\nSo be patient! Allah’s promise is indeed true. Whether We show you a part of what We promise them, or take you away [before that], [in any case] they will be brought back to Us.\nوَلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا رُسُلًا مِّنْ قَبْلِكَ مِنْهُمْ مَّنْ قَصَصْنَا عَلَيْكَ وَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ لَّمْ نَقْصُصْ عَلَيْكَؕ وَمَا كَانَ لِرَسُوْلٍ اَنْ يَّاْتِىَ بِاٰيَةٍ اِلَّا بِاِذْنِ اللّٰه‌ِۚ فَاِذَا جَآءَ اَمْرُ اللّٰهِ قُضِىَ بِالْحَقِّ وَخَسِرَ هُنَالِكَ الْمُبْطِلُوْنَ‏(78)\nWA LAQAD ARSALNAA ROSOLAM MIN QABLEKA MINHUM MAN QASASNAA A’LAYKA WA MINHUM MAL LAM NAQSUS A’LAYK, WA MAA KAANA LE-RASOOLIN AN-Y YAATEYA BE-AAYATIN ILLAA BE-IZNIL LAAH, FA-EZAA JAAA-A AMRUL LAAHE QOZEYA BIL-HAQQE WA KHASERA HONAALEKAL MUBTELOON.\nCertainly We have sent apostles before you. Of them are those We have recounted to you, and of them are those We have not recounted to you. An apostle may not bring any sign except by Allah’s permission. Hence, when Allah’s edict comes, judgment is made with justice, and it is thence that the falsifiers become losers.\nاَللّٰهُ الَّذِىْ جَعَلَ لَكُمُ الْاَنْعَامَ لِتَرْكَبُوْا مِنْهَا وَمِنْهَا تَاْكُلُوْنَ‏(79)\nALLAAHUL LAZEE JA-A’LA LAKOMUL AN-A’AMA LE-TARKABOO MINHAA WA MINHAA TAAKOLOON.\nIt is Allah who created the cattle for you that you may ride some of them, and some of them you eat;\nوَلَكُمْ فِيْهَا مَنَافِعُ وَ لِتَبْلُغُوْا عَلَيْهَا حَاجَةً فِىْ صُدُوْرِكُمْ وَعَلَيْهَا وَعَلَى الْفُلْكِ تُحْمَلُوْنَؕ‏(80)\nWA LAKUM FEEHAA MANAAFE-O’ WA LE-TABLOGHOO A’LAYHAA HAAJATAN FEE SODOOREKUM WA A’LAYHAA WA A’LAL FULKE TOHMALOON.\nand there are [numerous] uses in them for you, and that over them you may satisfy any need that is in your breasts, and you are carried on them and on ships.\nوَيُرِيْكُمْ اٰيٰتِهٖ ۖ  فَاَىَّ اٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ تُنْكِرُوْنَ‏(81)\nWA YOREEKUM AAYAATEH, FA-AYYA AAYAATIL LAAHE TUNKEROON.\nHe shows you His signs. So which of the signs of Allah do you deny?\nاَفَلَمْ يَسِيْرُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ فَيَنْظُرُوْا كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْؕ كَانُوْۤا اَكْثَرَ مِنْهُمْ وَاَشَدَّ قُوَّةً وَّ اٰثَارًا فِى الْاَرْضِ فَمَاۤ اَغْنٰى عَنْهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يَكْسِبُوْنَ‏(82)\nAFALAM YASEEROO FIL ARZE FA-YANZOROO KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATUL LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM, KAANOO AKSARA MINHUM WA ASHADDA QUWWATANW WA AASAARAN FIL ARZE FAMAA AGHNAA A’NHUM MAA KAANOO YAKSEBOON.\nHave they not travelled over the land so that they may observe how was the fate of those who were before them? They were more numerous than them and were greater [than them] in power and with respect to the effects [they left] in the land. But what they used to earn did not avail them.\nفَلَمَّا جَآءَتْهُمْ رُسُلُهُمْ بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ فَرِحُوْا بِمَا عِنْدَهُمْ مِّنَ الْعِلْمِ وَحَاقَ بِهِمْ مَّا كَانُوْا بِهٖ يَسْتَهْزِءُوْنَ‏(83)\nFALAMMAA JAAA-ATHUM ROSOLOHUM BIL-BAYYENAATE FAREHOO BEMAA I’NDAHUM MENAL I’LME WA HAAQA BEHIM MAA KAANOO BEHI YASTAHZE-OON.\nWhen their apostles brought them manifest proofs, they boasted about the knowledge they possessed, but they were besieged by what they used to deride.\nفَلَمَّا رَاَوْا بَاْسَنَا قَالُوْۤا اٰمَنَّا بِاللّٰهِ وَحْدَهٗ وَكَفَرْنَا بِمَا كُنَّا بِهٖ مُشْرِكِيْنَ‏(84)\nFALAMMAA RA-AW BAASANAA QAALOO AAMANNAA BIL-LAAHE WAHDAHU WA KAFARNAA BEMAA KUNNAA BEHI MUSHREKEEN.\nThen, when they sighted Our punishment, they said, ‘We believe in Allah alone, and disavow what we used to take as His partners.’\nفَلَمْ يَكُ يَنْفَعُهُمْ اِيْمَانُهُمْ لَمَّا رَاَوْا بَاْسَنَا ؕ سُنَّتَ اللّٰهِ الَّتِىْ قَدْ خَلَتْ فِىْ عِبَادِهٖ‌ۚ وَخَسِرَ هُنَالِكَ الْكٰفِرُوْنَ‏(85)\nFALAM YAKO YANFA-O’HUM EEMAANOHUM LAMMAA RA-AW BAASANAA, SUNNATAL LAAHIL LATEE QAD KHALAT FEE E’BAADEH, WA KHASERA HONAALEKAL KAAFEROON.\nBut their faith was of no benefit to them when they sighted Our punishment—Allah’s precedent, which has passed among His servants, and it is thence that the faithless will be losers.",
  "merits": "Surah al-Mo’min (The Believer) Or Surah Ghaafir\nThis is a ‘Makki’ Surah and it has 85 verses. When a person recites this Surah then the souls of all the Prophet (a.s.), the truthful people and the believers send salutations to him and pray for his forgiveness. Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that whoever recites this Surah once in every three days, his sins will be forgiven and he will become a God-fearing person.\nIt is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that if this Surah is written and kept in a garden or farm, then the plants or crops will become more fruit bearing and green. If kept in a business premises then business will prosper and more profit will be gained. Keeping this Surah as a talisman works as a cure for wounds and scars. This Surah is also a remedy for heart problems, dizziness and nausea."
}
